        "original_id": "ae250d68-3de4-504b-8692-9c88516e6935",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Choirboys\n- People: Robert Aldrich, Christopher Knopf, Joseph Wambaugh, Charles Durning, Louis Gossett, Jr., Randy Quaid, James Woods\n- Companies: Universal Pictures\n- Topics: American comedy-drama films, ensemble casts, film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Durning was born on February 28, 1923, and he became an American actor with appearances in over 200 movies, television shows, and plays.\n- The Choirboys is a 1977 American comedy-drama film directed by Robert Aldrich and written by Christopher Knopf and Joseph Wambaugh.\n- The Choirboys was based on Joseph Wambaugh's novel of the same title.\n- The Choirboys features an ensemble cast including Charles Durning, Louis Gossett, Jr., Randy Quaid, and James Woods.\n- Universal Pictures released The Choirboys to theaters on December 23, 1977.\n- Charles Durning died on December 24, 2012.",
